# Build context is the whole repo (`COPY . .`), so anything that would break
# `npm ci` or poison the compiled `.next` has to be excluded.

# Dependencies are installed inside the image from the lockfile, never copied
# from the host — a host node_modules (possibly pnpm, possibly arm64) would make
# the image non-reproducible and would break `npm prune --omit=dev`.
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# A host `.next` must never leak in: `next build` would reuse mismatched caches
# and the image would ship artifacts built from someone else's tree. This is the
# exact hazard AGENTS.md warns about ("never run `next build` during dev").
.next
next-env.d.ts

# Repo-local agent state and hives.
.hive
.hive2
omp-web-out
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.swp

# CI config is not needed to build the image, and copying it in would invalidate
# the source layer on every workflow tweak.
.github

# Docs and scratch files.
*.md
!AGENTS.md
LICENSE*